    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build. \n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a new owner which isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and the response reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`).\n\nFollowing the existing `bulkSignupWarning` response-only-flag pattern, I:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two `@Transient` response-only fields with accessors: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them by name automatically.\n\n3. **`PossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 the shared soft-match rule: scans `OwnerRepository.findAll()` for an existing owner (excluding self by id) with the same normalized last name (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) and same postcode but a *different* normalized E.164 telephone, returning the lowest matching id for determinism. A possible match requires the owner to have a postcode.\n\n4. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 an OfficeFloor function step that applies the rule and mutates the owner in place.\n\n5. **Pipelines** \u2014 wired the step into both `owners.POST.yml` (after save/`bulkWarning`, under `transaction`) and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` (under `readonly-transaction`), mirroring how `FlagBulkSignup` is recomputed on both create and fetch so the GET read-back returns the flags.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate`) and the full `mvn test` build pass green.",
