        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the established owner-pipeline conventions:\n\n- **`FlagPossibleDuplicate` mirrors `FlagBulkSignup` precisely** \u2014 a response-only flag populator that mutates the loaded owner in place and is wired identically into both the create (`transaction`) and fetch (`readonly-transaction`) pipelines. Same shape, same naming, same javadoc idiom.\n- **`PossibleDuplicate` follows the \"single source of truth helper\" pattern** used by `OwnerIdentity`, `OwnerTelephone`, `OwnerEmail`, and `OwnerPostcode`: a `final` package-private class with a private constructor and a static rule method, defined once so create and fetch agree. The rule/function split (helper `PossibleDuplicate.matchOf` + pipeline function `FlagPossibleDuplicate`) parallels `OwnerIdentity.of` + `ValidateUniqueIdentity` exactly.\n- **Reuse rather than duplication** \u2014 it correctly delegates telephone comparison to `OwnerTelephone.normalize` instead of re-implementing it. The local `normalizeName`/`normalizePostcode` helpers are equality-normalization specific to the soft match and don't duplicate anything existing (`OwnerPostcode` is a validity check, not an equality normalizer; there is no pre-existing name normalizer).\n- **Model fields mirror `bulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 two `@Transient` fields plus accessors, with javadoc matching the surrounding response-only derived-field style.\n- **OpenAPI additions follow the existing `readOnly` field convention** for `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\nNothing is in the wrong unit, no class is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer of this codebase would find the layout natural."
      }
